<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gavrilo Princip</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1894">1894</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gavrilo Princip was a Bosnian Serb nationalist who assassinated Archduke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archduke-franz-ferdinand-of-austria">Franz Ferdinand</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarajevo">Sarajevo</a> on 28 June 1914. The assassination triggered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/july-crisis">July Crisis</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, which led to the destruction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gavrilo-princip.jpg" alt="Gavrilo Princip" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gavrilo_Princip,_cell,_headshot,_bw_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The assassination of the heir to the throne, Archduke Franz Ferdinand, in Sarajevo on 28 June 1914 by the Bosnian Serb nationalist <b>Gavrilo Princip</b> triggered the July Crisis that produced the First World War.</blockquote><a href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Gavrilo Princip</b> shot the heir to the Austro-Hungarian throne and his wife Sophie.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-28">28 June in history</a></li><li><blockquote>On 28 June 1914 <b>Gavrilo Princip</b> assassinated Archduke Franz Ferdinand in Sarajevo.</blockquote><a href="/state/bosnia-and-herzegovina-austro-hungarian">Bosnia and Herzegovina (Austro-Hungarian)</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Obljaj, in what is now <a href="/countries/bosnia-and-herzegovina">Bosnia and Herzegovina</a>. Died in Theresienstadt Small Fortress, in what is now <a href="/countries/czech-republic">the Czech Republic</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=44.18,16.39&amp;year=1909" aria-label="Obljaj on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4942 600 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Gavrilo Princip"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5392 870h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5392 870h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=44.18,16.39&amp;year=1909">What was here in 1909? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
